    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d275">

                <pb facs="0322" n="316" sameAs="frus:frus1942v03/pg316"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/26284: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hayes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-12-05T22:00:00+01:00">December 5,
                            1942—10 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 6—2:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1969. Your 1362, December 4, 7 p.m. We have no evidence the reports are true.
                    Ministry of the Army denied similar reports last week. I am seeing the Foreign
                    Minister Monday<anchor n="73" xml:id="d275-f1"/> and shall then discuss the
                    matter with him.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hayes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
